{"ts":"2026-03-11T01:29:28.640Z","role":"ai","text":"All within limits (SKILL.md 239 lines, workflow SKILL.md 245 lines — both ≤250).\n\nHere's what was applied:\n\n**`process.md` — Stage 4a/4b:**\n- Added explicit warning: don't rely on plan mode's implicit behavior — always open with a full-coverage instruction\n- Added self-verification pass at 4b: check draft plan against every AC before writing the artifact\n\n**`work-queue/SKILL.md` — Stage Contracts table:**\n- 4a row: `EnterPlanMode` + **explicit coverage instruction** → text draft → `ExitPlanMode`\n- 4b row: Draft plan spec + **self-verification pass** + HTML artifact\n\n**`work-queue-workflow/SKILL.md` — Start-to-Finish Chain step 3:**\n- Added the ~15-point coverage degradation note as a hard reminder\n- Both the explicit instruction pattern and the AC verification pass are now baked in\n\nThe net effect: our Stage 4a now captures the key insight from the benchmark — plan mode is a useful structural gate, but the quality instruction has to be explicit. The mode alone doesn't make the model plan comprehensively.","session":"7602f476-1cf7-49a5-9cc5-f5a2c569539c"}
